{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-8311387317c8", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump halts new Iran strikes, cites deal", "summary": "Trump says the US and Israel will pause new attacks on Iran if a deal to end the war is reached rapidly; Tehran has not confirmed.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/no-new-iran-strikes-for-now-amid-deal-hopes-trump/live-78201442", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Trump said early Sunday (2 August) that the United States and Israel had agreed to hold off on a new wave of attacks against Iran, on condition that a deal to end the war is reached \"rapidly.\" In a post on his own platform, the US president said Iran and other regional states had asked him to pause after he had earlier declared Washington \"locked and loaded,\" and claimed \"the perimeters of a deal has been agreed to\" — a deal he said would require the \"immediate, complete and total\" reopening of the Strait of Hormuz and an end to Iran's nuclear programme. Tehran has not confirmed any agreement, no mediator or terms were disclosed, and the strait critical to global energy shipping remains closed; Iran has separately vowed a \"decisive response\" to any new strikes. This is day 156 of the conflict, and reporting notes Washington is contending with depleting stocks of Patriot interceptor missiles. Treat the \"deal\" framing cautiously: it rests on the US president's word alone.", "why": "A pause — if it holds — would be the first real de-escalation in a five-month war that has shut the Strait of Hormuz and driven up jet-fuel and energy prices in Europe. But an unconfirmed, terms-free announcement from one side is not a ceasefire, and a US shortfall of interceptors is the same constraint squeezing both Israel's and Ukraine's air defences.", "thread_id": "2026-08-02-news-trump-halts-new-iran-strikes-cites-deal", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-02", "event_date": "2026-08-02", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "United States", "Israel", "Strait of Hormuz"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-trump-halts-new-iran-strikes-cites-deal"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-8311387317c8", "edition": "2026-08-02-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Trump said early Sunday (2 August) that the United States and Israel had agreed to hold off on a new wave of attacks against Iran, on condition that a deal to end the war is reached \"rapidly.\" In a post on his own platform, the US president said Iran and other regional states had asked him to pause after he had earlier declared Washington \"locked and loaded,\" and claimed \"the perimeters of a deal has been agreed to\" — a deal he said would require the \"immediate, complete and total\" reopening of the Strait of Hormuz and an end to Iran's nuclear programme. Tehran has not confirmed any agreement, no mediator or terms were disclosed, and the strait critical to global energy shipping remains closed; Iran has separately vowed a \"decisive response\" to any new strikes. This is day 156 of the conflict, and reporting notes Washington is contending with depleting stocks of Patriot interceptor missiles. Treat the \"deal\" framing cautiously: it rests on the US president's word alone.", "why": "A pause — if it holds — would be the first real de-escalation in a five-month war that has shut the Strait of Hormuz and driven up jet-fuel and energy prices in Europe. But an unconfirmed, terms-free announcement from one side is not a ceasefire, and a US shortfall of interceptors is the same constraint squeezing both Israel's and Ukraine's air defences.", "importance": 3, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-d57bd6ddc2c1", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Ukraine, Russia trade port and refinery strikes", "summary": "Kyiv says it struck a Russian refinery and airfield while Russia hit Odesa and Mykolaiv ports; deadly strikes on Kyiv killed at least nine as Zelensky decried a Patriot shortage.", "url": "https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260801-russian-forces-strike-targets-in-ukraine-odesa-mykolaiv-ports", "source_domain": "france24.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Russia and Ukraine traded long-range strikes over the weekend, and Kyiv again pressed its shortage of Patriot interceptors. Ukraine said it hit a Russian oil refinery and a military airfield, while Russia said it bombed the Black Sea ports of Odesa and Mykolaiv on Saturday (1 August); Ukrainian officials reported at least nine dead and more than 30 injured after Russian strikes on Kyiv, with President Volodymyr Zelensky publicly lamenting a lack of Patriot air-defence missiles. Separately, a homemade bomb killed three people — including a woman said to be the bomber — and wounded 15 at an upscale Moscow restaurant on Saturday night.", "why": "The interceptor squeeze ties Kyiv's front directly to the Iran war — the same scarce US Patriot rounds are being rationed across two theatres at once.", "thread_id": "2026-05-20-cyber-papers-russia-ukraine-largest-aerial-campaign-of-the-wa", "first_seen_date": "2026-05-20", "event_date": "2026-08-01", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Odesa", "Volodymyr Zelensky"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-ukraine-russia-trade-port-and-refinery-strikes"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-d57bd6ddc2c1", "edition": "2026-08-02-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Russia and Ukraine traded long-range strikes over the weekend, and Kyiv again pressed its shortage of Patriot interceptors. Ukraine said it hit a Russian oil refinery and a military airfield, while Russia said it bombed the Black Sea ports of Odesa and Mykolaiv on Saturday (1 August); Ukrainian officials reported at least nine dead and more than 30 injured after Russian strikes on Kyiv, with President Volodymyr Zelensky publicly lamenting a lack of Patriot air-defence missiles. Separately, a homemade bomb killed three people — including a woman said to be the bomber — and wounded 15 at an upscale Moscow restaurant on Saturday night.", "why": "The interceptor squeeze ties Kyiv's front directly to the Iran war — the same scarce US Patriot rounds are being rationed across two theatres at once.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-8e4bd1268bf2", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Hungary shuts sole nuclear plant in heatwave", "summary": "Record-low Danube water from heatwaves forced Hungary to take the Paks nuclear plant offline for the first time in 44 years.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/canicule-pour-la-premiere-fois-la-hongrie-arrete-sa-centrale-nucleaire", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Hungary took its only nuclear power station offline for the first time in 44 years after successive heatwaves dropped the Danube too low to cool it. The government announced the shutdown of the Paks plant on Sunday (2 August), blaming record-low water levels; the plant supplies close to half the country's electricity, raising the prospect of a power crunch, and Germany's Rhine has fallen far enough to hamper river freight.", "why": "Europe's 2026 heat is now knocking out baseload power, not just straining it — a concrete example of climate stress hitting the electricity grid, with the same low rivers slowing coal and cargo along the Rhine.", "thread_id": "2026-08-02-news-hungary-shuts-sole-nuclear-plant-in-heatwave", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-02", "event_date": "2026-08-02", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Hungary", "Paks Nuclear Power Plant", "Danube"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-hungary-shuts-sole-nuclear-plant-in-heatwave"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-8e4bd1268bf2", "edition": "2026-08-02-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Hungary took its only nuclear power station offline for the first time in 44 years after successive heatwaves dropped the Danube too low to cool it. The government announced the shutdown of the Paks plant on Sunday (2 August), blaming record-low water levels; the plant supplies close to half the country's electricity, raising the prospect of a power crunch, and Germany's Rhine has fallen far enough to hamper river freight.", "why": "Europe's 2026 heat is now knocking out baseload power, not just straining it — a concrete example of climate stress hitting the electricity grid, with the same low rivers slowing coal and cargo along the Rhine.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-2cd8dab75cad", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Gansu flash floods kill dozens", "summary": "Flash floods in China's Gansu province killed dozens, with authorities opening an investigation amid landslide warnings.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/china-dozens-dead-in-gansu-flash-floods/a-78206328", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Flash floods in China's north-western Gansu province killed dozens over the weekend, and authorities opened an investigation as forecasters warned of further landslides. Continuing heavy rain has raised the risk of more slides in mountainous terrain, and the death toll was still being tallied.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-02-news-gansu-flash-floods-kill-dozens", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-02", "event_date": "2026-08-01", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["China", "Gansu"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-gansu-flash-floods-kill-dozens"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
