{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-005958f31543", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Federal Council cuts forest climate funds", "summary": "The Swiss Federal Council will scrap from 2027 the funds meant to adapt Swiss forests to climate change, drawing criticism from cantons and lawmakers.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/le-conseil-federal-coupe-les-fonds-destines-a-preparer-la-foret-suisse-au-changement-climatique", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The Federal Council will scrap, from 2027, the federal funds earmarked to help Swiss forests adapt to climate change — a decision drawing fire from cantons, lawmakers and wildfire specialists. The cut, attributed to environment minister Albert Rösti, removes the millions Bern had promised to convert forests toward more heat- and drought-resistant species, even as the 2026 heatwave accelerates tree die-off across the country. Critics say pulling the money now, mid-crisis, leaves cantons to shoulder adaptation alone.", "why": "Swiss forests do double duty as avalanche and rockfall protection and as carbon sinks; a funding gap during a record-hot summer is a bet that the adaptation bill can wait, one foresters dispute.", "thread_id": "2026-08-02-news-federal-council-cuts-forest-climate-funds", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-02", "event_date": "2026-08-02", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Switzerland", "Federal Council", "Albert Rösti"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-federal-council-cuts-forest-climate-funds"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-005958f31543", "edition": "2026-08-02-news", "fields": {"display_body": "The Federal Council will scrap, from 2027, the federal funds earmarked to help Swiss forests adapt to climate change — a decision drawing fire from cantons, lawmakers and wildfire specialists. The cut, attributed to environment minister Albert Rösti, removes the millions Bern had promised to convert forests toward more heat- and drought-resistant species, even as the 2026 heatwave accelerates tree die-off across the country. Critics say pulling the money now, mid-crisis, leaves cantons to shoulder adaptation alone.", "why": "Swiss forests do double duty as avalanche and rockfall protection and as carbon sinks; a funding gap during a record-hot summer is a bet that the adaptation bill can wait, one foresters dispute.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-0ef4e327ffd8", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Concacaf demands FIFA governance overhaul", "summary": "North American football confederation Concacaf demanded a complete overhaul of FIFA governance under Infantino after he withdrew a controversial World Cup restructuring plan.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/les-federations-de-football-d-amerique-du-nord-exigent-une-mise-a-plat-de-la-gouvernance-de-la-fifa-par-gianni-infantino", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Concacaf, the football confederation for North and Central America, demanded a \"complete overhaul\" of FIFA's governance under president Gianni Infantino. In a statement Saturday (1 August), the confederation accused the Zurich-based world governing body of operating \"outside any framework and without transparency,\" following the withdrawal of Infantino's contested plan to spin off the men's World Cup into a separate commercial entity. Separately, nominations for FIFA's next presidential election are open until 18 November, with few figures so far willing to challenge the incumbent.", "why": "FIFA is a Zurich-headquartered association under Swiss law, and open revolt from a founding confederation over its governance is the kind of dispute that periodically pulls in Swiss regulators and prosecutors.", "thread_id": "2026-08-02-news-concacaf-demands-fifa-governance-overhaul", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-02", "event_date": "2026-08-01", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FIFA", "Concacaf", "Gianni Infantino"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-concacaf-demands-fifa-governance-overhaul"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
{"ev": "publish", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "id": "st-0ef4e327ffd8", "edition": "2026-08-02-news", "fields": {"display_body": "Concacaf, the football confederation for North and Central America, demanded a \"complete overhaul\" of FIFA's governance under president Gianni Infantino. In a statement Saturday (1 August), the confederation accused the Zurich-based world governing body of operating \"outside any framework and without transparency,\" following the withdrawal of Infantino's contested plan to spin off the men's World Cup into a separate commercial entity. Separately, nominations for FIFA's next presidential election are open until 18 November, with few figures so far willing to challenge the incumbent.", "why": "FIFA is a Zurich-headquartered association under Swiss law, and open revolt from a founding confederation over its governance is the kind of dispute that periodically pulls in Swiss regulators and prosecutors.", "importance": 2, "status": "settled"}}
{"ev": "seen", "ts": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "actor": "news", "story": {"id": "st-44a566465f99", "date": "2026-08-02", "stream": "news", "headline": "Saint-Prex national-day barge catches fire", "summary": "The barge holding Saint-Prex's 1 August fireworks on Lake Geneva caught fire, setting off a chaotic display.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/a-saint-prex-sur-la-cote-vaudoise-la-barge-du-1er-aout-a-pris-feu", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "In Saint-Prex, on the Vaud shore of Lake Geneva, the barge carrying the town's 1 August fireworks caught fire on Saturday evening, setting off the rockets in a chaotic, unplanned burst. Instead of the traditional finale, spectators watched an anarchic salvo as the blaze on the barge ignited the pyrotechnics; the incident capped a National Day marked nationwide by heat and drought-related fire caution.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-08-02-news-saint-prex-national-day-barge-catches-fire", "first_seen_date": "2026-08-02", "event_date": "2026-08-01", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Saint-Prex", "Vaud"], "status": "settled", "first_seen": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "updated": "2026-08-02T10:10:20Z", "legacy_ids": ["2026-08-02-news-saint-prex-national-day-barge-catches-fire"], "editions": ["2026-08-02-news"], "origin": "writer:news", "streams": ["news"]}}
